/**
@page rutil_main The reSIProcate Utility Library (rutil)

rutil holds the general-purpose code that the SIP stack, the Dialog Usage
Manager and the other reSIProcate libraries are built on.  Very little of it
is SIP-specific; for SIP, see @ref resip_main and @ref dum_main.

@section rutil_strings Strings and Parsing
   - resip::Data is reSIProcate's string and byte-buffer class, used in place
     of std::string throughout the libraries.  It can share or borrow
     buffers instead of copying them, and has helpers for hex, base64,
     URL and XML encoding, and number conversion.
   - resip::ParseBuffer is a bounds-checked cursor over a buffer, used by
     all of the parsers.
   - resip::Inserter streams any container whose elements have operator<<.

@section rutil_threads Threads and Queues
   - resip::Mutex, resip::RecursiveMutex, resip::Lock and resip::Condition
     are now typedefs of std::mutex, std::recursive_mutex, std::unique_lock
     and std::condition_variable; resip::RWMutex, resip::ReadLock and
     resip::WriteLock provide reader/writer locking.
   - resip::ThreadIf wraps a std::thread with run(), shutdown() and join().
     It is kept for existing code; new code should use std::thread
     directly.
   - resip::Fifo and resip::TimeLimitFifo are the thread-safe message
     queues that the libraries use to pass messages between threads.

@section rutil_io Sockets and Event Loops
   - resip::FdPollGrp waits for socket events using epoll, poll() (WSAPoll()
     on Windows) or select(); resip::FdPollItemIf is the interface for a
     socket registered with it.
   - resip::SelectInterruptor wakes up a thread that is blocked waiting
     for socket events.
   - resip::GenericIPAddress, resip::DnsUtil and the cross-platform socket
     functions in Socket.hxx handle IPv4 and IPv6 addresses and sockets.

@section rutil_dns DNS
   The asynchronous DNS resolver used by the SIP stack lives in rutil/dns.
   resip::DnsStub caches results and runs queries for A, AAAA, SRV, NAPTR
   and CNAME records; it talks to the network through the resip::ExternalDns
   interface, which resip::AresDns implements using either c-ares or the
   bundled copy of ares.

@section rutil_logging Logging
   resip::Log is configured with resip::Log::initialize(), which can log to
   the console, syslog, a file or an application-supplied
   resip::ExternalLogger, with per-thread and per-subsystem levels.  Code
   logs through the StackLog, DebugLog, InfoLog, WarningLog, ErrLog and
   CritLog macros in Logger.hxx, each tagged with a resip::Subsystem.

@section rutil_misc Other Utilities
   - resip::Timer: millisecond and microsecond clocks and the SIP T1, T2
     and T4 timer values.
   - resip::Random: pseudo-random and cryptographically secure random
     values, in raw, hex and base64 form.
   - resip::ConfigParse: reads the command line and name = value
     configuration files used by repro, reTurn and the other servers.
   - resip::ServerProcess: daemonizing, PID files, signal handling and
     dropping privileges for those servers.
   - resip::DigestStream: computes MD5 and SHA digests through a
     std::ostream.
   - resip::OpenSSLInit: one-time OpenSSL setup, when built with OpenSSL.
   - resip::HepAgent: sends copies of SIP and RTCP traffic to a HEP
     (Homer) capture server.
*/
